    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.84), our two strongest plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a potent combination of a lead-off spot against Warren and a favorable park factor (+16%), while **Kyle Tucker** maximizes his utility out of the cleanup spot facing Houser. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.45) also present elite efficiency, with the latter serving as a critical source of speed despite facing an opposing starter in Sproat who manages the run game effectively. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.92) remains a plug-and-play staple; even against a tough arm like McClanahan, his elite xwOBA metrics and favorable platoon dynamics keep his daily floor high enough to warrant the UTIL slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Josh Jung** (55.03). While **Josh Jung** possesses strong underlying skills against a mid-tier xERA from Gallen, his overall efficiency score fell just short of the thresholds set by **Nolan Schanuel** and **Nasim Nunez**, whose lineup placement and platoon advantages narrowly edged him out for a starting spot. Managers should monitor the defensive efficiency of **Josh Lowe** and **Andy Pages** today; while both hover around a 60-point efficiency score, they face opposing catchers with sub-1.90s pop times, creating a slight downward pressure on their stolen base potential. We are proceeding with the current lineup, trusting that the aggressive baserunning profiles of **Sam Antonacci** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** will overcome the moderate risks presented by the opposing batteries today.",
